37. DORMANT ACCOUNT POLICY, POINT EXPIRY & INACTIVITY TIMER (180-DAY RULE)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TO MAINTAIN SYSTEM INTEGRITY AND OPTIMIZE WALLET NODES (`/users/{uid}`), A STRICT 
DORMANT ACCOUNT AND BALANCE EXPIRY POLICY IS ENFORCED:

  [A] 180-DAY INACTIVITY EXPIRED BALANCE: If a user account records ZERO login 
      activity, session re-authentication, or point transactions for a continuous 
      period of 180 consecutive days, the account shall be classified as "Dormant." 
      Upon reaching the 180th day of total inactivity, ALL accrued point balances 
      and wallet units shall automatically expire, forfeit, and be permanently 
      deducted (cleared to zero balance).

  [B] INACTIVITY TIMER RESET: The 180-day inactivity countdown automatically 
      resets back to zero whenever the user actively re-opens, logs into, or 
      authenticates their account before the 180-day limit expires.

  [C] PERMANENT LOSS UPON EXPIRY: Once points have expired due to 180 days of 
      inactivity, re-opening or re-authenticating the account will NOT restore 
      or recover the lost points. Unused balances that expire are permanently 
      extinguished and non-recoverable.

